WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.562
When several source columns become one value column, PostgreSQL needs a common data type.

00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:09.002
If one metric is integer and another is numeric, explicit casts may be helpful.

00:00:09.002 --> 00:00:13.472
The patient metric example casts selected values to numeric.

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:17.287
Do not let type coercion become an accidental part of the reshape.

00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:18.982
Choose the long value type deliberately.

00:00:18.982 --> 00:00:25.867
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.302
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:30.302 --> 00:00:36.482
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.482 --> 00:00:40.902
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:45.440
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
